<article class="env-lemma" id="0BJ3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BJ3">Lemma <span data-tag="0BJ3">16.4.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0BJ2" data-tag="0BJ2">16.4.1</a> Néron's blowup is functorial in the following sense </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
if $a \in A$, $a \not\in \mathfrak p$, then Néron's blowup of $A_ a$ is $A'_ a$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $B \to A$ is a surjection of flat finite type $R$-algebras with kernel $I$, then $A'$ is the quotient of $B'/IB'$ by its $\pi $-power torsion. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Both (1) and (2) are special cases of Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BIP" data-tag="0BIP">10.70.3</a>. In fact, whenever we have $A_1 \to A_2 \to \Lambda $ such that $\mathfrak p_1 A_2 = \mathfrak p_2$, we have that $A_2'$ is the quotient of $A_1' \otimes _{A_1} A_2$ by its $\pi $-power torsion. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>